# EtBadge Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtBadge` is a pill-shaped badge component for the eToro design system. It uses a compound component pattern for flexible composition, supporting:

- **Compound components**: `EtBadge.Label` and `EtBadge.Icon` subcomponents
- **Nine color variants**: neutral, red, orange, yellow, green, mint, blue, purple, violet
- **Two sizes**: medium (28px height), small (20px height)
- **Optional icons**: prefix, suffix, or both
- **Themed colors**: Automatically adapts to light/dark mode
- **Props injection**: Colors injected into children via `useComponentChildren` hook

**Does NOT handle:**

- Interactive states (not pressable)
- Navigation logic

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtBadge` (main component)

```tsx
<EtBadge
  color?: BadgeColor            // default: 'neutral'
  size?: BadgeSize              // default: 'medium'
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {children}
</EtBadge>
```

**Children constraints:**

- Must contain at least one of: `EtBadge.Label` or `EtBadge.Icon`
- Can contain both `EtBadge.Label` and `EtBadge.Icon` in any order
- Order of children determines visual layout (icon before label = prefix icon)

### `EtBadge.Label`

```tsx
<EtBadge.Label
  style?: StyleProp<TextStyle>
>
  {ReactNode}
</EtBadge.Label>
```

**Behavior:**

- Automatically colored based on parent badge's `color` prop
- Uses `body-tiny-medium` text variant
- Receives color via injected props (no prop drilling needed)

### `EtBadge.Icon`

```tsx
<EtBadge.Icon
  name:IconName // required - icon from icon library
/>
```

**Behavior:**

- Automatically colored based on parent badge's `color` prop
- Fixed size: 12px
- Receives color via injected props (no prop drilling needed)

### Types

| Type         | Values                                                                                                              |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `BadgeColor` | `'neutral'` \| `'red'` \| `'orange'` \| `'yellow'` \| `'green'` \| `'mint'` \| `'blue'` \| `'purple'` \| `'violet'` |
| `BadgeSize`  | `'medium'` \| `'small'`                                                                                             |

## Usage Patterns

### Basic usage

```tsx
<EtBadge color="green">
  <EtBadge.Label>New</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
```

### With prefix icon

```tsx
<EtBadge color="green">
  <EtBadge.Icon name="heart" />
  <EtBadge.Label>Favorites</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
```

### With suffix icon

```tsx
<EtBadge color="neutral">
  <EtBadge.Label>More</EtBadge.Label>
  <EtBadge.Icon name="chevronRight" />
</EtBadge>
```

### With both icons

```tsx
<EtBadge color="purple">
  <EtBadge.Icon name="heart" />
  <EtBadge.Label>Featured</EtBadge.Label>
  <EtBadge.Icon name="chevronRight" />
</EtBadge>
```

### Different sizes

```tsx
<EtBadge size="medium" color="blue">
  <EtBadge.Label>Default</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>

<EtBadge size="small" color="blue">
  <EtBadge.Label>Compact</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
```

### Status indicators

```tsx
<EtBadge color="green">
  <EtBadge.Label>Success</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
<EtBadge color="orange">
  <EtBadge.Label>Warning</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
<EtBadge color="red">
  <EtBadge.Label>Error</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
<EtBadge color="blue">
  <EtBadge.Label>Info</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
```

### Multiple badges in a row

```tsx
<View style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 8 }}>
  <EtBadge color="neutral">
    <EtBadge.Label>Draft</EtBadge.Label>
  </EtBadge>
  <EtBadge color="yellow">
    <EtBadge.Label>Pending</EtBadge.Label>
  </EtBadge>
  <EtBadge color="green">
    <EtBadge.Label>Active</EtBadge.Label>
  </EtBadge>
</View>
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using string children (not supported)

```tsx
// BAD - EtBadge doesn't support string shorthand
<EtBadge color="green">Success</EtBadge>
```

**Fix:** Always use compound components:

```tsx
<EtBadge color="green">
  <EtBadge.Label>Success</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
```

### ❌ Using subcomponents outside EtBadge

```tsx
// BAD - will render without color
<EtBadge.Label>Label</EtBadge.Label>

// BAD - will render without color
<EtBadge.Icon name="heart" />
```

**Fix:** Always wrap subcomponents inside `<EtBadge>` to receive proper colors.

### ❌ Using badge for interactive elements

```tsx
// BAD - Badge is not pressable
<Pressable>
  <EtBadge color="green">
    <EtBadge.Label>Click me</EtBadge.Label>
  </EtBadge>
</Pressable>
```

**Fix:** Use a button or chip component for interactive elements.

### ❌ Using very long labels

```tsx
// BAD - Badge is designed for short labels
<EtBadge color="neutral">
  <EtBadge.Label>This is a very long label that will look bad</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
```

**Fix:** Keep labels concise (1-2 words recommended).

### ❌ Manually styling colors

```tsx
// BAD - bypasses design system
<EtBadge.Label style={{ color: 'red' }}>Label</EtBadge.Label>
```

**Fix:** Colors are automatically managed based on badge `color` prop via injected props.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useBadgeColors` - hook providing themed colors (encapsulates `useEtoroTheme`)
- `useComponentChildren` - hook that injects props into children via `cloneElement`
- `EtText` - underlying text component for `EtBadge.Label`
- `EtoroIcon` - underlying icon component for `EtBadge.Icon`

### External Dependencies

- `react-native` - `View`, `StyleSheet`

### Design System Integration

Text-color resolution per variant in [`utils/get-badge-colors.ts`](utils/get-badge-colors.ts) is **partially migrated to V2**:

| Variant | V1 token | V2 token |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `neutral` | `textSecondaryNeutral` | `carbon500` |
| `red` | `statusNegative` | `verdictNegative600` |
| `green` | `statusPositive` | `verdictPositive600` |
| `orange` | `statusOrange` | (not migrated — V1 retained) |
| `yellow` | `statusYellow` | (not migrated — V1 retained) |
| `mint` | `statusMint` | (not migrated — V1 retained) |
| `blue` | `statusBlue` | (not migrated — V1 retained) |
| `purple` | `statusPurple` | (not migrated — V1 retained) |
| `violet` | `statusViolet` | (not migrated — V1 retained) |

The 6 color-family variants (orange/yellow/mint/blue/purple/violet) keep their V1 `status*` text tokens because the V2 palette (`carbon`/`primary`/`verdict`) does not yet provide equivalents for those color families. They will migrate when the V2 palette is extended.

Background fills (`backgrounds` map in `get-badge-colors.ts`) are sourced directly from primitive opacity scales (e.g. `greenOpacity['400.2']`) and are not theme tokens, so they are unaffected by the V1/V2 migration.

## Props Injection Architecture

The badge uses `React.cloneElement` to inject props into children:

- `useComponentChildren` hook clones children and injects `textColor` prop
- `EtBadge.Label` and `EtBadge.Icon` receive `textColor` as an injected prop
- This eliminates the need for context while keeping the API clean

**File structure:**

```text
hooks/
├── use-component-children.tsx  # Hook for injecting props into children
└── index.ts

subcomponents/
├── badge-label.tsx       # EtBadge.Label component
├── badge-icon.tsx        # EtBadge.Icon component
└── index.ts
```

## Sizing Specs

| Size   | Height    | Horizontal Padding | Vertical Padding | Icon Size |
| ------ | --------- | ------------------ | ---------------- | --------- |
| Medium | X7 (28px) | 10px               | X1 (4px)         | 12px      |
| Small  | X5 (20px) | 10px               | 0px              | 12px      |

- Border radius: X5 (20px, pill shape)
- Gap between children: HALF (2px)
- Font: Body/Tiny/Medium (12px, weight 500)
- Uses spacing constants from `core/styles/spacing` where applicable

## Accessibility

Built-in accessibility support:

- `accessibilityRole="text"`
- Custom `accessibilityLabel` can be provided
- `testID` prop for testing

